packages.prompt:
MOTION TRANSFER from @Video1.
Keep the original motion, timing, cuts, camera angle, camera movement, framing and performance of @Video1 exactly; every beat stays one to one: the table-level camera, the line of figures dancing across the table, the limbo under the chopsticks and the climb up the glass stem.
@Image1 — LEAD: the grey proxy figures of @Video1 become the zombie troupe from @Image1: flat black cut-out silhouettes about 5 cm tall with a thin phosphorescent lime-green outline, no eyes, no mouths, no clothes; three lurching zombies with bent, raised arms in a staggering zombie walk, one crouched, and one small black hand that walks on its fingers. Transfer this entire look to every proxy, one zombie per proxy, the smallest proxy becoming the hand; retain only the choreography, blocking and timing from @Video1. Their feet stay in contact with the tabletop.
@Image2 — LOCATION: rebuild the whole environment as shown in @Image2, with its light direction: a Tokyo apartment dining table after dinner at night, lit only by cold blue moonlight from the window on the left, with two glasses of red wine, chopsticks resting on a chopstick rest, a black screw cap lying on the table and the bottle. The bottle is exactly the bottle in @Image2: dark glass Bordeaux bottle, black screw cap, bright yellow front label framed top and bottom by black-and-yellow diagonal caution stripes, four black zombie silhouettes in a row (three lurching zombies in profile with bent, raised arms in a staggering zombie walk and one crouched) plus a small black hand rising from the ground, the name in dark red gothic blackletter and the word RIOJA below it. Keep the label geometry, colours, stripes and silhouettes exactly as @Image2; the cap is a screw cap, never a cork; the bottle never moves, tilts or changes shape, size or colour; no text is added. The bottle, the glasses and the chopsticks take the places of the matching proxies in @Video1 at the same scale, the figures about 5 cm tall against the bottle.
GLOW LOCK: in the dark only the thin outlines of the zombie silhouettes and the small hand glow a soft phosphorescent lime green, like real glow-in-the-dark ink: a thin luminous edge with gentle falloff, no neon tube look, no bloom halo, no lens flare. The label text and stripes do not glow; the yellow label reads as dark grey-green in the dark.
@Image3 — STYLE: @Image3 defines the visual style only: stylized 3D animation with graphic comic-book shading, halftone dots in the shadows, bold ink edge lines, subtle misregistered colour fringes, neon magenta and cyan rim lights over deep night blue, cinematic depth of field; do not copy its content, characters or layout.
Camera and framing: @Video1 alone defines angle, height, trajectory and lens perspective.
Screen direction never flips; each figure keeps the source's screen position and apparent scale; the window and moon stay on the left.
Match the video's sharpness and motion timing; render everything in the stylized 3D comic look, the label crisp and readable.
Avoid: identity drift between figures, extra figures, extra bottles, a cork, candles, faces or eyes on the zombies, neon tube glow, bloom halos, lens flares, glowing label text, a bottle that moves or changes, changed choreography, new camera moves, floating feet, added text, captions, logos or watermarks, people in the room.
